CR-0001 | Project-agnostic naming and examples | accepted | FR-09 | No project-specific service/env/CI-tool names anywhere; generic placeholders only; multi-CI-tool framing | @docs/cr/CR-0001-generic-project-agnostic.md
CR-0002 | Four named views (Detailed/Compact/Glance/Focus) + per-view attribute picker | accepted | FR-12,FR-02,FR-03,FR-07 | Four named views from header segmented control + per-view attribute picker; localStorage-persisted; full-attribute disclosure on history drawer + Focus-expanded rows | @docs/cr/CR-0002-four-named-views-and-attribute-picker.md
CR-0003 | Tree topology + three-layout axis (Matrix/Swim-lane/Workflow-rows) | accepted (Matrix-as-MVP-layout superseded by CR-0007) | FR-13,NFR-09 | DAG-of-env-edges per service; deployment_id required + parent_deployments optional; correlationAttribute picker; topology.edges on wire; SSE carries slot updates only | @docs/cr/CR-0003-tree-topology-and-layout-axis.md
CR-0004 | Optional ref + sha fields on deployment payload | accepted | FR-05 | Two new nullable string fields (ref, sha) on POST /api/deployments; surfaced on read wire; backward compatible with seven-field payload | @docs/cr/CR-0004-ref-and-sha-optional-fields.md
CR-0005 | ref/sha exposed as Display picker + Topology correlation options | accepted | FR-12,FR-13 | ref+sha become attribute-picker options on every view (per-view caps unchanged) and allowed values for correlationAttribute picker | @docs/cr/CR-0005-ref-sha-display-and-topology.md
CR-0006 | Light/Dark/Auto theme axis | accepted | NFR-09,new theme axis | Header gear popover; localStorage.dashboard.theme; default auto follows OS prefers-color-scheme; orthogonal to View+Layout; palette-only change; single-writer ThemeService post-bootstrap | @docs/cr/CR-0006-light-dark-auto-theme.md
CR-0007 | Defer Matrix layout from MVP to Phase 2.0 | accepted | FR-13 | FR-13 reduced to Swim-lane + Workflow-rows for MVP; default flips to Swim-lane; Matrix-layout templates removed; wire shape unchanged; Matrix returns in Phase 2.0 | @docs/cr/CR-0007-defer-matrix-layout-to-phase-2.md
CR-0008 | Standardised API validation + ProblemDetails + OpenAPI + Scalar UI | accepted | FR-05,new validation+OpenAPI axes | Length-only validation via DataAnnotations on DTO; RFC-7807 ValidationProblemDetails on all 4xx; OpenAPI 3.x at /openapi/v1.json (Microsoft.AspNetCore.OpenApi); Scalar at /scalar (Scalar.AspNetCore) | @docs/cr/CR-0008-api-validation-and-openapi-scalar.md
CR-0009 | Optional pull-mode fetcher (Dashboard.Fetcher) + universal X-Progress-Reporter event-attribution header | proposed | FR-05/FR-10,SAD §3/§7/§9/§10,CR-0008,CR-0003 | Universal X-Progress-Reporter request header (cap 64 non-whitespace) on POST /api/deployments + REQUIRED on new GET/PUT /api/fetcher/state/{source-id} cursor endpoints; persisted to new progress_reporter VARCHAR(64) NULL column; surfaced on every Read event-attribute surface; pull-mode framed as strict subset of push-mode (one ingest path, one auth model, one attribution mechanism); new fetcher_state table (PK (progress_reporter,source_id), cursor VARCHAR(4096), updated_at); Dashboard.Fetcher library + Dashboard.Fetcher.Host (Microsoft.NET.Sdk.Worker) + deployment-dashboard-fetcher container image; MVP: GHA adapter only + opt-in --profile fetcher local-dev + ACR image publish; ACA+Terraform deferred; pairs with ADR-0004 (4 cursor/process/adapter decisions); amends CR-0008 verbatim with header row and CR-0003 with wire-shape note; route registered as catch-all ({**sourceId}) to support source-ids with slashes (owner/repo); §3d endpoint list amended 2026-05-20 (paired with ADR-0007 + issue #19) — adds GET /repos/{o}/{r}/actions/runs/{run_id} (run metadata for workflow path + head_sha) + GET /repos/{o}/{r}/actions/runs/{run_id}/jobs + GET /repos/{o}/{r}/contents/.github/workflows/{path}?ref={head_sha} so GHA adapter can emit needs:-derived intra-run + per-env-predecessor parent_deployments edges against the YAML *as the run saw it* (vs. as it is now on the default branch); all three endpoints cacheable per cycle; silent-degrade with INFO log on failure (no edges from affected signal; cycle does not fail); timing inference between parallel jobs explicitly rejected per ADR-0007 | @docs/cr/CR-0009-pull-mode-fetcher-and-progress-reporter.md
CR-0010 | Component CI pipeline (GitHub Actions — build, test, package) | accepted (Phase 7 doc-amend pass; as-built on PR #2 head 39641b5) | SAD §9 outbound,WBS §1.5.8 split,WBS §5.1 split,WBS §1.6 new | Hybrid topology - 4 thin workflows (api/fetcher/frontend/gateway.yml) + 1 reusable _build-and-push-image.yml (Option A; build-kind:dotnet|static); 5th caller demo-gha.yml added by CR-0013 (baked demo-gha image); demo-driver.yml caller added by CR-0013 §3e amendment (per issue #46); identical trigger matrix (push:main / pr:main / tags v* / workflow_dispatch); CI-only (no deploy); container images only (no NuGet/npm); GHCR today via GITHUB_TOKEN (deviates from CR-0009 implicit ACR expectation per NFR-06+NFR-02 rationale); deterministic tags (sha-<7> always, latest on default-branch push, pr-<N>-sha-<7> on PR built-not-pushed, vX.Y.Z+vX.Y on tag push); blocking gates: dotnet format, ng lint, dotnet/ng test, mockup-visual; non-blocking: coverage; concurrency cancel-in-progress per github.ref; least-privilege permissions (caller: contents:read+packages:write+id-token:write; per-job overrides on reusable); reusable MUST NOT declare top-level permissions (Phase 5 amendment); EF migration script artefact retired (ef-migrations-script-<sha>) by ADR-0009 (API self-migrates on startup; api.yml emit-migration-artefact:true removed; release.yml migration.sql asset upload removed); dogfooding hook to .github/actions/notify/ posted to dashboard; PR=build-only, push=build+test+push; scripts.yml (issue #7) follows the same sibling-thin-workflow shape (trigger matrix + concurrency + permissions:contents:read) but is verification-only (Pester + bats; no image build, no GHCR push) | @docs/cr/CR-0010-component-ci-pipeline.md
CR-0011 | Fetcher rate-limit governance: configurable self-imposed cap + usage reporting endpoints + dashboard surfacing | proposed | FR-10,CR-0009,ADR-0008 | Two new env vars (FETCHER_RATE_LIMIT_ABSOLUTE / FETCHER_RATE_LIMIT_PERCENTAGE); leaky-bucket cap on observed upstream Remaining (ADR-0008 Decision 1); POST /api/fetcher/usage (Write-gated; fetcher pushes per tick) + GET /api/fetcher/usage (Read; returns latest snapshot per (adapter_id,source_id); 200 empty-array when no fetcher); in-memory IFetcherUsageCache singleton + re-publish-on-tick (ADR-0008 Decision 2; no EF entity/table/migration); right-aligned rate-limit cluster in dashboard stats strip (severity bands 0-60% green / 60-85% amber / >85% red; stale-affordance fires when now-received_at > 2×poll_interval; NFR-09 reflow invariant + collapse threshold; pairs with ADR-0008 Decision 3 per-token cap + Decision 4 upstream_used field name) | @docs/cr/CR-0011-fetcher-rate-limit-governance.md
CR-0012 | Integration test substrate: WireMock.Net mock-gha service + testing/integration/ suite + demo-bundle co-location | accepted (2026-05-22) | issue #10,CR-0009,ADR-0004 | mock-gha standalone container (pinned sheyenrath/wiremock.net:2.4.0; integration compose profile; no host port except under integration profile per NFR-04); fetcher retargeted via GHA_API_BASE_URL=http://mock-gha:80; testing/integration/ xUnit cross-stack runner (FETCHER_POLL_INTERVAL_SECONDS=1 for NFR-03 5s envelope); fixture corpus at testing/fixtures/gha/ (mappings/ + scenarios/<state-id>/ + scenarios/_cross-cutting/ + demo/); 6 canonical box states from ui-states.yaml drive scenario bundles; admin API surface: POST /__admin/mappings/import + POST /__admin/mappings/reset + GET /__admin/requests; demo-bundle co-located under testing/fixtures/gha/demo/ (not wired until CR-0013); integration.yml CI workflow starts non-blocking then promotes to blocking after one calendar week of green runs | @docs/cr/CR-0012-integration-test-substrate.md
CR-0013 | Demo-mode default in release-install entrypoint: installer flag inversion + demo Compose profile + baked demo-gha image + realistic bundle content + dynamic-mock scenario walk | accepted (2026-05-22) | issue #44,CR-0012,CR-0010,ADR-0009 | Installer default inverted from empty-stack to demo-stack; flag matrix: (no flag)=demo, -RealGha/--real-gha=real GHA upstream (renamed from -Fetcher), -Empty/--empty=bare stack, -Demo/--demo=back-compat alias; baked first-party demo-gha image ghcr.io/.../deployment-dashboard-demo-gha:${DASHBOARD_VERSION} (5th component image; gateway/demo-gha/Dockerfile; built by demo-gha.yml CR-0010 caller); demo bundle: 6 services x 5+ envs / 30-36 slots / 80-150 deployments; demo Compose profile co-exists with integration profile (different services: demo-gha vs mock-gha; fetcher retargeted per GHA_API_BASE_URL); demo-driver Python sidecar (gateway/demo-driver/) added by §3e amendment per issue #46 for live scenario walk; demo-driver.yml workflow caller added; DASHBOARD_VERSION substitution pins demo-gha image to same tag as api/fetcher/frontend/gateway | @docs/cr/CR-0013-demo-mode-default-installer.md
